  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#39282\", \"PowerToys#32852\", \"PowerToys#28490\"], \"answer\": \"This feature (scheduling a shutdown/sleep after a set number of minutes) has been requested before and is tracked as a duplicate of the earlier scheduled shutdown/sleep requests (#17970, #28490). PowerToys has no such tool yet, so please upvote the existing request. In the meantime, use the built-in command: press Win+R and run `shutdown /s /t X`, where X is the number of seconds (e.g. 1800 for 30 minutes). Use `shutdown /a` to cancel. You can also create a shortcut (.lnk) to shutdown.exe with the timer parameter, or trigger it with Task Scheduler. For sleep, use Task Scheduler or a script, as shutdown.exe does not directly do sleep.\"}",
